course: dictionary
lesson: 15854
title: Words that signal surprise
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Unexpectedly is built from three parts: un- (not), expect (think something will happen), and -ly (in a way). So it means in a way that nobody thought would happen. «Unexpectedly, the door opened.» Nobody was waiting for the door to open, so the word tells you something surprising has happened.
explain: You will meet this word in stories as a twist. «The dog was asleep until, unexpectedly, it leapt up and barked.» The writer uses unexpectedly to warn you that the story is about to change direction.
explain: You also use it in real life. «The bus arrived unexpectedly, so we had to run.» Visitors can arrive unexpectedly, and the weather can change unexpectedly. In science, a result can turn out unexpectedly, and that often leads to new questions.
fact: Unexpectedly means in a way that nobody expected or planned.
fact: Unexpectedly is an adverb, so it tells us how something happened.
fact: «Quite unexpectedly» means very suddenly and surprisingly.
fact: «Not unexpectedly» means «as expected», so the thing was predicted.
fact: Unexpectedly is often used to signal a twist in a story.
exercise: «The door opened unexpectedly.» What does unexpectedly mean here? | *In a way nobody planned | On purpose, as part of a plan | Slowly and carefully | Very loudly, like a bang
exercise: What does «not unexpectedly» mean? | By accident | Never again | *As expected | Quite surprisingly
exercise: «The rain came unexpectedly, so we had no coats.» Find and copy the adverb that tells how the rain came. | coats | *unexpectedly | came | rain
test: «Unexpectedly, the lights went out in the middle of the film.» What is the best meaning? | The lights went out because someone planned a party | The lights were turned on slowly every evening | *The lights went out in a way nobody had planned | The film was too long to watch
test: Which sentence shows something happening unexpectedly? | The shop opens at nine every day | We planned the picnic for Sunday | *A cat jumped onto the table when nobody had called it | The bell rang at the usual time
exam: Which word is the best swap for unexpectedly in «The visitors arrived unexpectedly»? | Every day | On purpose | *Without warning | Carefully
